      "heading": "Blackjack rules",
      "backgroundColor": "#080E0B",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "AT THE TABLE Blackjack rules Get as close to 21 as you can without going over. Each player competes against the dealer. 01 Know your cards Number cards count at face value. Jacks, queens, and kings count as 10. An ace counts as 1 or 11, whichever keeps your hand at 21 or less. An ace and a 10-value card in your first two cards is a natural Blackjack. 02 Choose your move After placing a bet, choose to hit for another card or stand with your total. When allowed, you can also double down, split a pair, or surrender half your bet. Go over 21 and your hand busts. The dealer plays after everyone fin",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    }
